# The published tree mirrors the working copy, with two exceptions, both forced
# by GitHub's 100 MiB per-blob limit (104,857,600 bytes).  A push containing a
# larger blob is rejected as a whole, so these two can never be stored here.
#
# .venv/            local virtualenv, ~200 MB of pip-installed third-party
#                   libraries.  Rebuilt by `python -m venv .venv` followed by
#                   `pip install -r requirements.txt`; its largest blob,
#                   frida/_frida.pyd, is 112.5 MiB on its own.
# backups/base.apk  a 100.3 MiB capture sample.

/.venv/
/backups/base.apk
